      "caveat": "Real-world progression-free survival: from the start of the first Treatment [SUBTYPE=Immuno] record to the first Diagnosis event after it with PROGRESSION in Y / Yes, or death. Progression read from the record (in MSK-CHORD, from notes by NLP) is only as complete as that recording; events on the anchor's own day are not counted. Censored at the last follow-up, which is OS_MONTHS × 30.4375 days on the timeline's clock; death is OS_STATUS 1:DECEASED. That OS_MONTHS counts from the timeline's day 0 was checked on these patients: 0 of 2,632 anchored patients have a timeline event more than 31 days past it (a study above 5% is refused). Left truncation as in the survival view: a patient whose anchor falls before day 0 enters the risk set at day 0. Left out: 5102 cohort patients with no Treatment [SUBTYPE=Immuno] record, 0 with no follow-up after it, and 283 anchored before day 0 whose endpoint also came before it, so were never at risk. Medians with 95% intervals from the Greenwood band on the log scale. 2-group log-rank (1 df). Treated patients are not randomised: the cohorts can differ in who was offered the treatment, when, and how sick they were, so a difference here is an association. Each site sends only (entry, time, event) counts."
